  {
   "topic": "System",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A wire is crimped into an SPH contact, the contact is pushed into a PHR housing, and the housing plugs onto a PH header soldered to the board."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Contact choice",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "SPH-004T-P0.5S takes fine wire (AWG #32 to #28); SPH-002T-P0.5S takes AWG #30 to #24. SPH-002T-P0.5L covers AWG #28 to #24 with lower insertion force, at the cost of vibration resistance and with a different crimp height."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board layout, through-hole",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Holes are φ0.7 +0.1/0 on a 2 mm pitch, ±0.05 non-cumulative. The right hole size depends on board material and drilling; a glass-cloth (hard) laminate may need a larger hole. Layouts are shown from the side the connector mounts on."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board layout, SMT",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Signal lands sit on a 2 mm pitch, ±0.05 non-cumulative, with a reinforcement land at each end for the tin-plated copper-alloy reinforcement. Layouts are shown from the side the connector mounts on; figures are for reference."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Circuit 1 is marked on the header body. Headers carry an (LF)(SN) label."
  }
